# Operator-only mirror-sync tooling. Tracked here, in the private repo, so it has
# history and survives a lost machine. It never reaches the public mirror, and that
# is enforced where it can actually be checked: `scripts` is in the sync script's
# WITHHOLD list, and its own `held` gate counts any withheld path appearing in a
# public commit and refuses to push while the count is above zero. Ignoring the
# directory here only ever kept it out of the backup.

# Local test scratch: adversarial cert fixtures + audit notes (never commit).
/s.p7
/c.bin
/s*.crt
/s*.csr
/audit/
/adversarial-review/

# Coding-agent instructions and local editor config. Operator-side only: these
# describe how we work on the repo, not the product, and the public mirror is
# built from tracked files, so keeping them untracked keeps them out of it.
/CLAUDE.md
/AGENTS.md
/GEMINI.md
/.cursor/

# Conformance vector signing keys. The vectors are published; the throwaway CA
# that issued them is not, and the publication gate rejects any key file outright.
spec/vectors/.keys/
